# Local secrets. The build stage runs `COPY . .`, so without these a developer's DATABASE_URL and
# VERSE_AUTH_SECRET are baked into a build layer, where they survive in the image's history even
# though the final distroless stage copies only named paths and never ships them.
#
# The glob covers every .env variant rather than the file alone, because .env.local and .env.production
# are the ones that actually hold real values, and forgetting one of them is the failure this is here
# to prevent.
.env
.env.*
